<!-- page: calls.html -->

Page 1 of 2 · your calls

# One call is yours, one waits on the caterer, and the menu day is settled

The cutoff is yours to set. The second list waits on the caterer. The menu day was settled on 2026-11-18.

## Call 1: when do orders close? [open · Sam]

**Today:** orders close when the caterer phones, at about 10:45. The office places 38 orders a day.

| Option | Buys | What changes, and for whom | Cost |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| A · 10:30 | The caterer gets the full list an hour before it cooks. | Staff who arrive after 10:30 miss lunch that day. | Nothing to build; one email to staff. |
| B · 11:00 | Late arrivals can still order. | The caterer cooks from a list 30 minutes later, and asked for 45 minutes of warning. | A second call to the caterer each day. |

**Pick (open): A.** The caterer's lead time decides it, and few orders come after 10:30. **Measure after the ruling:** count orders refused after the cutoff for two weeks. **Reverse:** if more than 1 in 10 orders is refused, move to B.

**The caterer's lead time decides the cutoff; the late arrivals are the cost.**

## R1: does the caterer take a second list? [waiting · the caterer]

A refused order costs about 2 lunches a week.

| Option | Buys | What changes, and for whom | Cost |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| A · Yes | Late orders get lunch. | Sam sends two lists a day. | A fee per second list. |
| B · No | One list, one call. | Late orders are refused, as today. | None. |

**Pick (waiting on the caterer): A.** It is the only option that feeds the late arrivals. **Reverse:** if the fee is over the cost of one lunch, pick B.

**Only a second list feeds the late arrivals.**

## Small calls

| Call | State | Options, and what each means | Pick |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **S1 ·** Which day does the menu change? | [settled · Sam] | **Monday:** The week starts with a new menu. **Friday:** Staff see next week's menu before the weekend. **Ruling, 2026-11-18, Sam:** Monday, as the caterer asked. It replaces the ruling on call S0. | Monday. It matches the caterer's own week. |
| **S0 ·** Does the menu change every week? | [settled · replaced] | **Weekly:** A new menu each week. **Monthly:** One menu a month. **Ruling, 2026-10-02, Sam:** Weekly. | Weekly. |

**Both small calls are settled, and neither waits on you.**

**How the late share was counted**

Orders stamped after 10:30, over all orders, for two working weeks: 4 in 100.

