Page 2 of 2 · how an order travels

# An order passes four stages, and each has one owner

An order goes from staff to the list, to the kitchen, to the desk. A late order stops at the list.

## The stages

[Figure: **Each of the four stages has one owner, so a late order has one person to ask.**]

Text alternative: Four stages left to right on a wide screen, top to bottom on a narrow one, each with its owner. Order (staff), List (Sam), Kitchen (caterer), Desk (Sam).

Still frame: stills/how-figure-stages.png

## Who a late order reaches

[Figure: **Only a late order on a menu-change day reaches nobody.**]

Text alternative: A grid of order time against menu day. On time on any day reaches the caterer; late on a normal day reaches Sam; late on a menu-change day reaches nobody.

Still frame: stills/how-figure-matrix.png

## One late order, step by step

[Figure: **An order placed at 10:40 is refused at the list, before the caterer sees it.**]

Text alternative: A stepper over one late order. Its still frame shows the refusal at the list.

Still frame: stills/how-figure-stepper.png

## Today's timings

| Stage | Owner | Closes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Order | Staff | 10:30 |
| List | Sam | 10:30 |
| Kitchen | Caterer | 11:15 |

**The list closes with the orders, so nothing waits between them.**

